From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: single-line comments where the stack added multi-line ones

The lean gate (tools/zig/lean_check.py on the pin and on the patched tree,
each from inside its own tree, diffed by lean_new.py) counted 11 problems the
pin does not have, all "multi-line comment": 9 in glm_l2pf.cu's header (0032),
1 in glm_glue_bmm.cuh above router16 (0038) and 1 on ringsAgree in
cuda_prompt_pair.zig (0042). Each block becomes one comment line, with the
rest of what it said moved onto the code lines it describes. No code changes.

Receipt: scripts/lean.sh work/pin/tree <tree> printed "127 problems, 116 on
the base, 11 new" before this patch (5,941 files against 5,991).

diff --git a/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_bmm.cuh b/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_bmm.cuh
--- a/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_bmm.cuh
+++ b/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_glue_bmm.cuh
@@ -428,8 +428,7 @@
 }  // namespace glm_bmm
 
 // TF_GLM_OVN_ROUTER16 (decode, up to 16 rows): 16 x 32 a block, each warp one 16 x 8 tile, ST stages (glue.py's bm 16).
-// Every output's chain is tf_glm_router_tile's: one mma per 16 inputs from zero, K ascending in its slice.
-namespace glm_bmm {
+namespace glm_bmm {  // every output's chain is tf_glm_router_tile's: one mma per 16 inputs from zero, K ascending
 template <int ST>
 __device__ __forceinline__ void router16(const __nv_bfloat16* x, const __nv_bfloat16* w, float* part, int64_t rows,
                                          int64_t x_stride, int64_t d, int64_t ne, int ks) {
